1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:04,366
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Thirty-Eight.

2
00:00:04,366 --> 00:00:09,409
Triangles on equal bases and in the same parallels are equal in area.

3
00:00:09,409 --> 00:00:17,813
Let triangles A B C and D E F stand on equal bases B C and E F and lie between the same parallel lines B F and A D.

4
00:00:17,813 --> 00:00:22,490
We prove that triangle A B C is equal in area to triangle D E F.

5
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:26,528
Extend segment A D in both directions to points G and H.

6
00:00:26,528 --> 00:00:35,960
By Proposition Thirty-One, through point B draw segment B G parallel to segment C A, and through point F draw segment F H parallel to segment D E.

7
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:45,769
Then each of the figures G B C A and D E F H is a parallelogram on equal bases B C and E F and between the same parallels B F and G H.

8
00:00:45,769 --> 00:00:52,145
By Proposition Thirty-Six, parallelogram G B C A is equal in area to parallelogram D E F H.

9
00:00:52,145 --> 00:01:01,044
By Proposition Thirty-Four, the diagonal A B bisects parallelogram G B C A, so triangle A B C is half of parallelogram G B C A.

10
00:01:01,044 --> 00:01:08,681
Likewise, the diagonal D F bisects parallelogram D E F H, so triangle D E F is half of parallelogram D E F H.

11
00:01:08,681 --> 00:01:18,140
Since the halves of equal things are equal to one another, triangle A B C is equal in area to triangle D E F, as was required to prove.
